    <version>0.11.1</version>
    <time>1785872224</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.11.1

Upstream fixes a segfault, a hang and around thirty further bugs across all
four I/O backends.

Packaging: switched to the PyPI sdist because upstream did not bump the
version in pyproject.toml for 0.11.0/0.11.1, so a build from the git tag
produced caio-0.10.2.dist-info. Also drops the top-level tests package that
upstream's wheel now installs into site-packages.</comment>
    <requestid>1369386</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>24a8e4b282a6cab0966caea59cde7b4a</srcmd5>
    <version>0.12.2</version>
    <time>1786026111</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-caio to 0.12.2.

- 0.11.2 adds io_uring SQPOLL support (on by default where the kernel offers it)
  plus deferred submission batching
- 0.12.0 makes all four backends safe under free-threaded CPython
- 0.12.1 fixes the broken 0.12.0 Linux wheels (cp313-cp313t tag does not exist)
- 0.12.2 stops thread_aio's thread pool on close() and moves the free-threading
  classifier to Beta

Built from the PyPI sdist as before. All seven tests the spec deselects still
exist in 0.12.2, so the %check skip list is unchanged; the one new test file
(test_free_threading.py) needs no additional build dependency.

Verified locally on aarch64/openSUSE_Tumbleweed: 135 passed, 503 skipped,
27 deselected; rpmlint 0 errors, 0 warnings; spec-cleaner diff empty;
source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1369632</requestid>
  </revision>
